              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "estco"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It's delicious. One bit of advice: the minute the almonds are brown, put them in a singer layer on a sheet of wax paper. I didn't do this the first time and they hardened in the pan. By the time I was able to get them out, I had almond dust!\nThe evening I served this, I had an apple tart for dessert so decided to use pears in the salad. I bought them several days in advance but they were still hard as rocks the day I needed them. I used red grapes cut in half instead and eliminated the dried cranberries. Everyone loved it.",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-23T23:15:48.697Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bmoss"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Every time I make salad for friends or family it is a hit. I have substituted blue cheese with feta too. Always a go to salad!",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-11T03:54:04.423Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "maggete"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My family loves this salad! We usually go half and half red leaf and spinach, and usually substitute the almonds for pecans. We opt not to add sugar to the nuts, or the dressing as the salad is sweet and flavorful without it. We also prefer goat cheese rather than blue cheese.",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-01T14:25:47.337Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cinfrea"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was absolutely delicious! I halved the recipe because it was just my husband &amp; I. Should have made the full amount &amp; will do so next time. Only thing I changed was feta for the bleu cheese because that’s what I had on hand.",
            "datePublished": "2019-08-13T23:30:43.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rae of Hope"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made it, loved it, substituted cranberry cinnamon goat cheese in place of bleu cheese. Add dressing on the side or immediately before eating as red leaf lettuce tends to quickly become soggy with this combination of ingredients.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-01T12:52:09.277Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rachycez"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Flavorful &amp; hearty! Will definitely add this to my salad rotation. I made a couple of modifications to the dressing: - cut the sugar out completely, I felt the cranberries, sugared almonds and apples were sweet enough - reduced the oil to 2 Tbsp. since the avocado, cheese and nuts also blend in as oil/fat components when tossed I'm not a fan of blue cheese, so I used chevre goat cheese; red onion and baby field greens also worked great. Thanks for sharing this recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2009-11-24T11:17:06.560Z"
          },
          {
